  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative or shows early signs of pessimism (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 with recent declines).",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — if price rises sharply, model should not overreact and avoid overshoots.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly below recent 30-day average, gently raise it toward historical mean.",
    "When sentiment turns positive (e.g., 0.50 or above), allow forecast to rise slightly faster than historical trend, but cap growth to avoid overestimation.",
    "Correct for lag: if true outcome is rising while model is still lagging, adjust forecast upward by 5-10% of recent trend magnitude.",
    "Avoid overcorrection after sharp drops — if model overcorrects upward after a dip, reduce forecast by 10-15% to prevent volatility overcompensation."
  ]
}
